    "result": "I implemented both functions in `solution.py` and wrote a 28-test pytest suite in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` now passes all 28. `can_book` checks the rules in the spec's order: the two `ValueError` cases first, then same-day, the 4-hour limit, opening and closing hours, and finally conflicts. A booking conflicts unless it starts at least `buffer_minutes` after an existing booking ends or ends at least that long before one starts, which makes back-to-back bookings allowed when the buffer is 0. `merge_intervals` validates every interval, sorts a copy by start, and merges overlapping or touching intervals without modifying the input. One test failed on the first run because I had written the wrong expected value for the buffer boundary; I corrected the test, not the implementation. The only other file I created is `tests/test_solution.py`, and I installed nothing.",
